.TH HYPERWHISPER-COMPANIONCTL 1 "August 2026" "HyperWhisper" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hyperwhisper-companionctl \- manage optional desktop companions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hyperwhisper-companionctl
{install-gnome|remove-gnome|install-kde|remove-kde}
.SH DESCRIPTION
Installs, enables, or removes the HyperWhisper active-window companion for the
current desktop user. It must not be run as root. Debian package installation
does not invoke this command or modify user home directories.
.SH PRIVACY
Companions expose only process identifier, application identifier, and window
title through the documented session D-Bus contract.
